[{:db/id "q-98342/selection/fc3b63992da517118e36ed60a8a02b583ae43a0c8efce461bba7c3b204a7f3dc" :answer/id #uuid "a9ae433e-248f-5100-a081-dfb1ef3fe8ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98342/selection/cdb9921a1274667b5fa923d394a10f9a01019c9817bb69b37c42466af5600e3e" :answer/id #uuid "24be30f9-d8d7-5da8-bf5a-75c0a7cd1df8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.01" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98342/selection/756c4cadde78e35e93e196c1f547afe3ec64a73e12d42e0d14b603dfece653c4" :answer/id #uuid "738ed73d-b486-521e-ad84-9e1de1647447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98342/selection/e1d388869d547e201a97fe7efb531ec58fe08ab67a57e96f7962e95aab1dba54" :answer/id #uuid "c2cc5401-76ab-5776-a2e9-af41f884cc7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.99" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98342/selection/af6ef4cb3d0c064ff3b62922264f6b85bd8171eb004860a2d53ed6f6ae538ef9" :answer/id #uuid "cfa07642-7da2-524c-b6b8-94ba1ac508af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98342/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e5ed355-6a4f-5c4a-8d01-a99e4ac83ef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98342/selection/756c4cadde78e35e93e196c1f547afe3ec64a73e12d42e0d14b603dfece653c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-98342/selection/fc3b63992da517118e36ed60a8a02b583ae43a0c8efce461bba7c3b204a7f3dc" "q-98342/selection/cdb9921a1274667b5fa923d394a10f9a01019c9817bb69b37c42466af5600e3e" "q-98342/selection/756c4cadde78e35e93e196c1f547afe3ec64a73e12d42e0d14b603dfece653c4" "q-98342/selection/e1d388869d547e201a97fe7efb531ec58fe08ab67a57e96f7962e95aab1dba54" "q-98342/selection/af6ef4cb3d0c064ff3b62922264f6b85bd8171eb004860a2d53ed6f6ae538ef9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98342" :question/id #uuid "164023df-d37c-516f-9c3b-868f9fb8729b" :question/math-academy-id "q-98342" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,2,3)=3,\\,{f}_{x}(1,2,3)=-2,\\,{f}_{y}(1,2,3)=1,\\,{f}_{z}(1,2,3)=3.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,3)$ estimate the value of $f(0.96,1.98,3.03).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,2,3)+∇f(1,2,3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =f(1,2,3)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,2,3),{f}_{y}(1,2,3),{f}_{z}(1,2,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =3+⟨-2,1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(0.96,1.98,3.03)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=0.96,$ $y=1.98,$ and $z=3.03$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.96,1.98,3.03) & ≈3+⟨-2,1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨0.96-1,1.98-2,3.03-3⟩ \\\\  & =3+⟨-2,1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.04,-0.02,0.03⟩ \\\\  & =3+0.08-0.02+0.09 \\\\  & =3.15\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-98342/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1639105-dca4-50d1-8d86-a7aed03ba0b5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98342"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98347/selection/05ed6945ee2963b514a1f8a35d2719a4a0912f7024a282d664c6890627d1f824" :answer/id #uuid "cbc5f628-a45c-512b-bd99-96cf15997590" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25.64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98347/selection/99788fa3aed377c6148bac726b36cfb6170c36eff1385c072a49f9bc30205982" :answer/id #uuid "e9b75960-4d46-5822-aa76-d3169239ed59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24.78" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98347/selection/66c7e058a6ad5b53b47a2ddd2a5aa038a987d68ff35fef15ed02510ef1a97a8f" :answer/id #uuid "1f19b13c-a104-52b1-96e2-d6ca0232a622" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24.85" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98347/selection/64f7d21a9eb45c0ec150a0bbe247f6a942e4e465e3f1cae0be423cc7570055bf" :answer/id #uuid "63814b85-18f2-54da-910c-a66a92fd2e57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25.06" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98347/selection/a564627a03404663305ce4b35b6bfd9628d13ce10cb47aa8d244f186ad3045bd" :answer/id #uuid "48504aa5-c3c9-54fc-98d4-9105583a03b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24.99" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98347/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a967a5f-c3be-5a15-b50f-2bcf02c1822c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98347/selection/a564627a03404663305ce4b35b6bfd9628d13ce10cb47aa8d244f186ad3045bd" :answer-field/choices ["q-98347/selection/05ed6945ee2963b514a1f8a35d2719a4a0912f7024a282d664c6890627d1f824" "q-98347/selection/99788fa3aed377c6148bac726b36cfb6170c36eff1385c072a49f9bc30205982" "q-98347/selection/66c7e058a6ad5b53b47a2ddd2a5aa038a987d68ff35fef15ed02510ef1a97a8f" "q-98347/selection/64f7d21a9eb45c0ec150a0bbe247f6a942e4e465e3f1cae0be423cc7570055bf" "q-98347/selection/a564627a03404663305ce4b35b6bfd9628d13ce10cb47aa8d244f186ad3045bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98347" :question/id #uuid "a6fb78aa-f2e7-500d-a880-3c8ff234bc2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-98347" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & f(3,0,4)=25, &  & {f}_{x}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, \\\\  & {f}_{y}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, &  & {f}_{z}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,0,4),$ estimate the value of $f(3.01,0.1,3.99).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,0,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(3,0,4)+∇f(3,0,4)\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-0,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =25+⟨{f}_{x}(3,0,4),{f}_{y}(3,0,4),{f}_{z}(3,0,4)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y,z-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(3,0,4)$, ${f}_{y}(3,0,4)$ and ${f}_{z}(3,0,4),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(3)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=3 \\\\ {f}_{y}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(0)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=0 \\\\ {f}_{z}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(4)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈25+⟨3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y,z-4⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(3.01,0.1,3.99)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=3.01,y=0.1$ and $z=3.99,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.01,0.1,3.99) & ≈25+⟨3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨3.01-3,0.1,3.99-4⟩ \\\\  & =25+⟨3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,0.1,-0.01⟩ \\\\  & =25+0.03-0.04 \\\\  & =24.99\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98347/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1639105-dca4-50d1-8d86-a7aed03ba0b5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129654/selection/0b4d0904423beae0fde4cc108bfe7419d5613edaee8ddd34dc32b0cd436729a2" :answer/id #uuid "500899d9-3be0-5e5a-911c-4af664d0adcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.88" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129654/selection/fe5bc2409c7b88dfc8bda3c065c2bb97d1f667e0ef91f48d68d2f9b973df63dc" :answer/id #uuid "0082ecdf-47e5-53a5-895e-7a4e03248e03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.93" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129654/selection/0135fb78cd3e94a68911506d8f8e792e5a15d84bf9b79e74bccf3eb124eba605" :answer/id #uuid "5e056001-1d92-5766-8006-b42dc59e54d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129654/selection/cad03aa4f0c66faf88f64a30efd31d3b7cfb5cd2fd8c6852ad3998e817cc1318" :answer/id #uuid "a407e943-1fcb-56c2-8166-77dc98c90d48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.09" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129654/selection/bc42be545d8e082697a22238be81ba3f0ade4bb21b6781bc9ea3caa7298852d2" :answer/id #uuid "5ad6384f-5c57-5f5b-8dad-fc88c4721a3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129654/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfb73485-902b-5d18-b9b9-048f28380e6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129654/selection/0b4d0904423beae0fde4cc108bfe7419d5613edaee8ddd34dc32b0cd436729a2" :answer-field/choices ["q-129654/selection/0b4d0904423beae0fde4cc108bfe7419d5613edaee8ddd34dc32b0cd436729a2" "q-129654/selection/fe5bc2409c7b88dfc8bda3c065c2bb97d1f667e0ef91f48d68d2f9b973df63dc" "q-129654/selection/0135fb78cd3e94a68911506d8f8e792e5a15d84bf9b79e74bccf3eb124eba605" "q-129654/selection/cad03aa4f0c66faf88f64a30efd31d3b7cfb5cd2fd8c6852ad3998e817cc1318" "q-129654/selection/bc42be545d8e082697a22238be81ba3f0ade4bb21b6781bc9ea3caa7298852d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129654" :question/id #uuid "e2824792-4fee-5f3f-be81-2e4b2980e7af" :question/math-academy-id "q-129654" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,0,-1)=1,\\,{f}_{x}(1,0,-1)=-1,\\,{f}_{y}(1,0,-1)=-1,\\,{f}_{z}(1,0,-1)=0.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,0,-1)$ estimate the value of $f(1.02,0.1,-0.96)$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,0,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,0,-1)+∇f(1,0,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-0,z-(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =f(1,0,-1)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,0,-1),{f}_{y}(1,0,-1),{f}_{z}(1,0,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y,z+1⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨-1,-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y,z+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.02,0.1,-0.96)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.02,$ $y=0.1,$ and $z=-0.96$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.02,0.1,-0.96) & ≈1+⟨-1,-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨1.02-1,0.1,-0.96+1⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨-1,-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0.02,0.1,0.04⟩ \\\\  & =1-1(0.02)-1(0.1)+0(0.04) \\\\  & =1-0.02-0.1+0 \\\\  & =0.88\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129654/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1639105-dca4-50d1-8d86-a7aed03ba0b5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129654"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129746/selection/21078b5fcc6797a69cd0e130849fe7d66df8ebd3e1d5906051583cdb774f61ab" :answer/id #uuid "9433909f-0111-5198-840d-ad8d8b2b1180" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈2x+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129746/selection/9762e95ab37dabed7f3b38c91e1eb848c3bddfedaeb9bad62e9260fa1eb5012d" :answer/id #uuid "dd3de839-b10f-5875-85e0-f384a2825ab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-2+2y+3z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129746/selection/1377e74f7813bb1aa59a660a1cc704f65165f3a48e920b0ddedbd91060db3f8e" :answer/id #uuid "7dd416d0-1ef2-51a8-93a4-3be0957eeb24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-3+2x-y+z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129746/selection/57aa68d08021b473b41f6f572251d2276610d478df9844b9bde48fc47990b0d7" :answer/id #uuid "3b318543-6d6b-5b8b-9bf4-82ed13590598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈1-x+y-z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129746/selection/ec5c9cfcba920b537ae9765bc4b974ec5de23f15e576a04ba559130fd0d9377f" :answer/id #uuid "b36d70c2-de52-5d60-94b9-f3ac92184afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-x-y-2z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129746/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2e319fa-8986-5bcf-b645-e666599902b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129746/selection/57aa68d08021b473b41f6f572251d2276610d478df9844b9bde48fc47990b0d7" :answer-field/choices ["q-129746/selection/21078b5fcc6797a69cd0e130849fe7d66df8ebd3e1d5906051583cdb774f61ab" "q-129746/selection/9762e95ab37dabed7f3b38c91e1eb848c3bddfedaeb9bad62e9260fa1eb5012d" "q-129746/selection/1377e74f7813bb1aa59a660a1cc704f65165f3a48e920b0ddedbd91060db3f8e" "q-129746/selection/57aa68d08021b473b41f6f572251d2276610d478df9844b9bde48fc47990b0d7" "q-129746/selection/ec5c9cfcba920b537ae9765bc4b974ec5de23f15e576a04ba559130fd0d9377f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129746" :question/id #uuid "9fed137c-3970-57b9-8c2b-495f775fd2ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-129746" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=yz-x.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,-1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(0,-1,1)+∇f(0,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x,y+1,z-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(0,-1,1)=-1.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-1\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(0,-1,1)=-1, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =z\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(0,-1,1)=1, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =y\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(0,-1,1)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(0,-1,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(0,-1,1) & =⟨{f}_{x}(0,-1,1),{f}_{y}(0,-1,1),{f}_{z}(0,-1,1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(0,-1,1)+∇f(0,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x,y+1,z-1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+⟨-1,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y+1,z-1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1-(x)+(y+1)-(z-1) \\\\  & ≈1-x+y-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-129746/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0015e19e-222b-5c5b-a020-93392c50c10e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129746"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
